    {
      "id": "iplomb1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.4 High Court of Andhra Pradesh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "57s28nx",
      "content": "After the bifurcation of the state in 2014, the High Court at Hyderabad was designated as the common High Court for both Andhra Pradesh and Telangana for a transitional period. The Andhra Pradesh Reorganisation Act provided for the establishment of a new High Court for Andhra Pradesh at Amaravati. The new High Court of Andhra Pradesh was established at Amaravati."
    },
    {
      "id": "mz3v0bi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.5 District Administration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l6ifljx",
      "content": "The district is the basic unit of administration in Andhra Pradesh. Each district is headed by the District Collector (an IAS officer) who oversees revenue administration, law and order, election management, and development activities. The district is sub-divided into revenue divisions, mandals (the basic administrative unit introduced in Andhra Pradesh in 1985 as a replacement for talukas), and villages."
    },
    {
      "id": "mu55v9z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.6 Local Self-Government"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gvgbzg4",
      "content": "Andhra Pradesh has a three-tier Panchayati Raj system introduced following the 73rd Constitutional Amendment. The three tiers are:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rivcsut",
      "content": "(a) Gram Panchayat – at the village level"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r56d23y",
      "content": "(b) Mandal Praja Parishad – at the mandal level"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional articles governing the powers, appointment, and discretionary functions of the Governor.",
        "Relationship and collective responsibility between the Chief Minister, Council of Ministers, and the State Legislature.",
        "Jurisdiction, writ powers, and structure of the High Court of Andhra Pradesh.",
        "73rd and 74th Constitutional Amendment Acts related to Local Self-Government institutions."
      ],
      "id": "68a5k78"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2oklry6",
      "content": "(c) Zilla Praja Parishad – at the district level"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fxkd4ht",
      "content": "Urban local bodies include Municipal Corporations, Municipalities, and Nagar Panchayats. Major municipal corporations include Greater Visakhapatnam Municipal Corporation (GVMC), Vijayawada Municipal Corporation, Guntur Municipal Corporation, Tirupati Municipal Corporation, and others."
    },
